hysics:\n\n- Sunlight is white light containing all colors (wavelengths).\n- When light enters the atmosphere, it hits tiny gas molecules (nitrogen, oxygen).\n- Shorter wavelengths (blue/violet) scatter much more than longer wavelengths (red/orange) — this is Rayleigh scattering, proportional to 1/λ⁴.\n- During the day, the sun is overhead, light travels a shorter path through the atmosphere. Blue light gets scattered in all directions, filling the sky.\n- At sunset, the sun is low, light travels a much longer path through the atmosphere. Most of the blue light gets scattered away before reaching your eyes, leaving the longer wavelengths (red, orange) to pass through.\n\nI should keep it simple, maybe use an analogy. Let me write a clear, warm explanation.\n</think>\n\n## Why the Sky Changes Color\n\n**The short version:** Sunlight is made of all the colors mixed together (that's why it looks white).","timing_ms":{"first_token":21453.272250,"per_token":[21453.272250,1155.831227,1161.969679,1160.440263,1155.961100,1157.889000,1161.686685,1167.209982,1169.233243,1166.111399,1165.874215,1159.027262,1159.047967,1169.756285,1163.123702,1161.593022,1164.141196,1161.090747,1167.304895,1173.968806,1170.030767,1169.053593,1170.110688,1168.980585,1162.338770,1173.267714,1170.934948,1167.486321,1174.773147,1166.164024,1171.139398,1177.070873,1197.024701,1168.822472,1165.464053,1167.454896,1174.579259,1173.168369,1168.345782,1169.702542,1169.187050,1169.040122,1178.334881,1166.520827,1174.775947,1174.741227,1170.150337,1169.767822,1179.947354,1174.096232,1169.831886,1174.851404,1168.612264,1170.795252,1182.181959,1177.964447,1170.949589,1168.526151,1175.880819,1177.148905,1169.345308,1177.414540,1177.588220,1169.172603,1178.097024,1184.666406,1177.025257,1178.837620,1181.805701,1171.928619,1175.925187,1183.227214,1186.348400,1176.116996,1171.547817,1180.946225,1184.546133,1183.975554,1184.829127,1179.719370,1175.519536,1178.117728,1183.089869,1182.851996,1174.913693,1179.526441